<article class="env-definition" id="03PW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03PW">Definition <span data-tag="03PW">59.35.1</span>.</a> Let $f: X\to Y$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $\mathcal{F} $ a presheaf of sets on $X_{\acute{e}tale}$. The <em>direct image</em>, or <em>pushforward</em> of $\mathcal{F}$ (under $f$) is </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  f_*\mathcal{F} : Y_{\acute{e}tale}^{opp} \longrightarrow \textit{Sets}, \quad (V/Y) \longmapsto \mathcal{F}(X \times _ Y V/X).  \]
</div>
  <p> We sometimes write $f_* = f_{small, *}$ to distinguish from other direct image functors (such as usual Zariski pushforward or $f_{big, *}$). </p>
</article>